// TEST: Unknown Unit Name In Derived RHS (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3015
// A `Unit` right-hand side composes names already in scope. A name that is
// neither a declared unit nor a built-in scale constant is a declaration-site
// error -- it used to warn to stderr and mint `turn` as a fresh BASE unit,
// which typechecks the misspelling into a dimension unrelated to `radian`
// and lets the program compile. `pii` is one letter off `pi`, so this is the
// exact shape the scale-constant spelling makes easy to hit.
Unit radian
Unit turn = 2 * pii * radian
